From 5dee606cb166d6baeaf227304d7479d31cce01fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gus bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:20:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] avcodec: add V4L2 Request API MPEG-4 Part 2 and H.263
 hwaccel

Add a stateless V4L2 Request API hwaccel for MPEG-4 Part 2 (Simple and
Advanced Simple profiles) and for H.263, for the
V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG4_SLICE and V4L2_PIX_FMT_H263_SLICE pixel formats and
the MPEG-4 stateless controls:

  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG4_VOL
  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG4_VOP
  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG4_QUANTISATION

One request is queued per coded VOP. The output buffer holds exactly
one VOP, from its start code to the next start code: the other headers
of the packet are left out and the VOPs of a packed bitstream are
queued one by one, as the decoder gets to them.

The VOL and VOP controls of the first picture are given to the driver
when the hwaccel is initialised, so that a driver which lacks a tool
the stream needs (global motion compensation, quarter sample, data
partitioning, an optional mode of H.263) makes the decoder fall back to
software. The modes of the H.263 picture header are passed as flags;
the driver decides.

The size of the H.263 picture header does not count what the decoder
reads of the first slice in the Slice Structured mode. A picture with a
custom picture format has source format 6, also when the decoder was
given the size by the container.

The decoders keep a few more header fields for this: the MPEG-4 decoder
video_object_layer_verid, obmc_disable, fixed_vop_rate and
reduced_resolution_vop_enable, the H.263 decoder whether the picture
header has PLUSPTYPE and a custom picture format.

The controls are not part of the kernel headers yet: a private copy of
their definitions is in v4l2-stateless-mpeg4.h.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
